  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Modern and environmentally friendly concrete casting systems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The economy in Bolivia, and particularly in Santa Cruz, is thriving. As a consequence the real estate market is booming and construction of medium to high rise buildings is increasing very strongly.High rise buildings are built with local expertise but local construction companies do not have the skills or access to modern technology. Particularly for buildings with more than 4 floors, the casting of concrete structures is currently completely inadequate.Casting in Bolivia is done by constructing a mould with wood, supported by wooden poles. Because wooden planks never have the same shape, the moulds are normally not straight and when used to cast a concrete floor or wall, an irregular surface is the result. Furthermore, the wooden moulds are often not strong enough to support the enormous weight of the concrete floor and many accidents happen during casting.In more developed countries, metal moulds are used with steel supports. These moulds are straight and strong, resulting in level floors/walls and strong concrete structures. When the design of the mould is well calculated, accidents and risks are minimal.Project partners, Rheto Arquitectos S.L. from Spain and Con4t S.R.L. from Santa Cruz, are proposing to introduce these modern casting methods, consisting of well calculated steel moulding systems, compliant with international building standards, in Bolivia.For this purpose, they will set up a new joint venture in Santa Cruz, which will offer state-of-the-art steel casting services to real estate developers and construction companies. This is completely new for Bolivia, and will significantly increase safety during construction of high rise buildings.</narrative>
  </description>
